by a drug in temporal microarray data: a case study</article-title><source>Proceedings of the Joint Statistical Meetings of the American Stastical Association.</source><year>2003</year><publisher-loc>Biopharm</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Student Paper Competition Award</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B39"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spellman</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Comprehensive identification of cell cycle-regulated genes of the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae by microarray hybridization</article-title><source>Mol. Biol. Cell</source><year>1998</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>3273</fpage><lpage>3297</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9843569</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B40"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vander Velden</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Peccoud</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Sanders</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>Ciardo</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modeling networks of molecular interactions in the living cell: structure, dynamics, and applications</article-title><source>Proceedings of the10th International Workshop on Petri Nets and Performance Models.</source><year>2003</year><publisher-loc>Washington, DC</publisher-loc><publisher-name>IEEE Computer Society</publisher-name><fpage>2</fpage><lpage>10</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B41"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><source>Stochastic Modelling for Systems Biology.</source><year>2006</year><publisher-loc>Boca Raton, Florida</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Taylor &#x00026; Francis</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B42"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zak</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Local identifiability: when can genetic networks be identified from microarray data?</article-title><source>Proceedings of the Third International Conference on Systems Biology</source><year>2002</year></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>